  "notes": "へぼい is an informal い-adjective meaning lousy, crappy, or incompetent. It comes from the noun へぼ (an unskilled person, a novice).\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverbial: へぼく\n- Negative: へぼくない\n- Past: へぼかった\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- へぼい{選手|せんしゅ}: a lousy player\n- へぼいミス: a stupid/clumsy mistake\n- {腕|うで}がへぼい: to be unskilled\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- しょぼい: shabby, pathetic (similar casual tone)\n- ダメ: no good (more general, less insulting)\n- {下手|へた}: unskillful (neutral, not rude)\n\nREGISTER:\nCasual and somewhat rude. Used when criticizing or complaining. Not appropriate in polite or formal settings. Can sound playful among friends but offensive directed at strangers.",
